# Diagrams

Use [Material diagrams](https://squidfunk.github.io/mkdocs-material/reference/diagrams/) when a relationship is clearer as a picture than as prose. A diagram is a fenced block with the `mermaid` language. The Mermaid fence is configured on `pymdownx.superfences`. Do not add custom JavaScript or an ELK layout.

Use only the types Material styles for light and dark mode: `graph`, `sequenceDiagram`, `stateDiagram-v2`, `classDiagram`, and `erDiagram`. Do not use pie charts, Gantt charts, user journeys, git graphs, or requirement diagrams.

````markdown
```mermaid
graph LR
  A[YAML template] --> B[Blocks]
  B --> C[PDF]
```
````

- `graph LR` flows left to right. `graph TD` flows top to bottom. Prefer `LR` for a short process and `TD` when the chart is narrow.
- Rectangles are steps (`A[Start]`), diamonds are decisions (`B{Error?}`), and edge labels use `-->|Yes|`.
- Keep a diagram to a handful of nodes so it stays readable on a phone.
- One diagram per idea. Do not repeat the same steps in the paragraph beside it.
